Changes for 2.0-0 (2026-11-17)
  * New function borm(): the Bayesian analog of rms::orm() (as blrm() is
    to rms::lrm()), supporting all 5 of orm()'s link families (logistic,
    probit, log-log, complementary log-log, Cauchy), exact censoring,
    pcontrast, and both the single- and dual-sigma (mix_re) random-
    intercept extensions of rms::orm.rfit(). Includes bormStats()/
    print.bormStats() for Spearman's rho and Somers' Dxy with highest
    posterior density intervals, following rms::orm()'s own censoring
    rules. See web/R/rmsb/borm_development.md for the full development
    history.
  * borm(): new yde/ytrans mechanism for Y-dependent
    (non-proportional-odds) effects, generalizing blrm()'s own ppo/cppo
    to allow more than one Y-dependent shape at once, with a combined
    beta+tau npcontrast for the Y-dependent effect. tausd, the prior SD
    for tau, is specified on a raw, portable scale -- one unit of the
    yde predictor, one SD of ytrans(y) -- rather than an internal,
    dataset-dependent one; default value unchanged.
  * print.borm()'s summary table reorganized: first column now shows
    Obs, Distinct Y, Median Y, p, Draws, Chains, Time (plus cluster/
    random-effect information when present); third column shows the
    mean |P(Y>=median)-0.5| index, matching rms::print.orm(), including
    its subscripted Y[0.5] formatting under prType='latex'/'html'.
  * blrm()/borm(): new cores_loo argument (default 1) to control loo()'s
    own parallelism separately from the mc.cores option; "loo failed"
    now reports the actual underlying error instead of a generic message.
  * blrm()/borm(): sampling.args's documentation now describes using
    adapt_delta/max_treedepth to address divergent transitions on hard,
    separation-prone data.
  * blrm(): fixed a bug where a user-supplied init= was silently ignored
    when backend='rstan'.
  * blrm(): Stan code now uses precomputed censoring subscripts from
    rms::ormIdx() (shared with borm()); fixed two related bugs found in
    the process -- a stale censoring-sentinel convention that could
    silently break censored fits, and a cppo left-censoring score that
    did not vary with the censoring bound.
  * blrm(): the unconstrained PPO model (ppo without cppo) with censored
    Y now errors informatively instead of silently corrupting the
    response.
  * blrm(): Ncens1/Ncens2 (matching rms::orm.fit()'s own convention)
    replace the old Ncens field in the fit object and in print.blrm() --
    not backward compatible with fits saved before this change.
  * blrm(): npcontrast's ycut argument now actually has an effect (was
    previously silently ignored); ycut may also be a named vector giving
    a different Y value per named setting.
  * blrm(): normcppo=TRUE now prints a warning when used with cppo,
    since it can distort the ordinary (non-PPO) coefficient for any
    predictor that also appears in the main formula.
  * blrm(): improved numerical accuracy of the interior/interval-censored
    log-likelihood terms in the constrained- and unconstrained-PPO Stan
    code.
  * DESCRIPTION: now requires rms >= 8.2-2.

Changes for 1.1-3 (2026-10-29)
   * blrm: added sampling.args to hash digest
   * print.blrm: changed to use new version of prModFit in rms
   * print.rmsb: fixed old bug related to rownames being lost with drop=TRUE which surfaced with one predictor and intercepts=FALSE
   * cluster: removed this function as it is now in the new, required rms package

Changes for 1.1-2 (2025-04-13)
   * predict.blrm: fixed type='fitted' for binary Y; thanks Christian Hametner: <https://discourse.datamethods.org/t/bayesian-regression-modeling-strategies/6105/99>
   * removed Ocens function which is now in rms 7.0
   * changed to be compatible with storage of functions in rms::probabilityFamilies
   * updated to use Ocens2ord on top of Ocens, needs rms 8.0-0

Changes for 1.1-1 (2024-07-07)
   * blrm: added argument showopt to show Stan optimizer steps, default is FALSE
   * blrm: added options(rmsbmsg=FALSE) to allow the user to suppress information messages
   * lrmconppot.stan: fixed bug for dim(C2) p -> q
   * replaced use of survival::survConcordance and Hmisc::somers2 with concordancefit

Changes for 1.1-0 (2024-03-11)
   * Store cppo as deparsed for opt object from optimization (MLE) to prevent huge environment from being carried along
   * blrm: Non-downward compatible changes: removed keepsep argument
   * blrm: Added npcontrast argument for specification of priors for non-proportional-odds parameters in the constrained partial PO model through the use of contrasts, parallel to pcontrast for the PO part of the model; changed 3 stan code modules for this

Changes for 1.0-0 (2023-09-26)
   * blrm: added support for cmdstan and cmdstanr package using backend=
   * When using cmdstan uses bayesplot package for pairs plots
   * stanDx: new code for cmdstan diagnostics
   * stackMI: corrected erroneous implementation of file= where it was only applying to one of the imputations; also handled generally the conversion of functions in fit object to character strings for efficient serializing
   * Added non-exported function cluster so as to not depend on survival package
   * blrm: added sampling.args argument
   * blrm: trapped ppairs error in case plot region too small to hold graph
   * blrm: added pcontrast argument for user-specified priors on linear combinations of regression coefficients; required changing all Stan code
   * blrm: removed priorsd argument (NON-DOWNWARD-COMPATIBLE CHANGE)

Changes for 0.1-0 (2022-04-12)
   * blrm: got around bug in model.response not keeping class Ocens
   * soprobMarkovOrdPost: removed since Hmisc has soprobMarkovOrdm
   * lrmconppot.stan: removed redundant pi simplex (thanks Mark Jones <mark.jones1@sydney.edu.au>

Changes for 0.0-2 (2021-02-27)
   * Removed @title lines from Roxygen comments
   * Enhanced predict.blrm and changed prediction methods to use it
   * Changed storage of cppo function in fit object to character strings so as to not have saveRDS serialize it with all its environment data
   * Added lrmconppot.stan to implement flat and t-distribution priors for intercepts
   * blrm: added iprior argument for lrmconppot
   * predict.blrm: fixed fun= with finint=FALSE
